WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.340 --> 00:00:01.060
Socialism,

00:00:01.060 --> 00:00:01.740
Nazism,

00:00:01.740 --> 00:00:03.180
progressivism,

00:00:03.180 --> 00:00:04.080
isms

00:00:04.080 --> 00:00:06.100
have done so much damage.

00:00:06.100 --> 00:00:08.140
But people still believe in them.

00:00:08.140 --> 00:00:09.060
Here is an outline

00:00:09.060 --> 00:00:10.900
of all the systems of government.

00:00:10.920 --> 00:00:11.720
Matt Kibbe

00:00:11.720 --> 00:00:13.180
made this video about

00:00:13.180 --> 00:00:14.600
the deadly isms.

00:00:14.620 --> 00:00:15.860
At the bottom,

00:00:15.860 --> 00:00:17.140
you'll see the worst types

00:00:17.140 --> 00:00:18.760
of totalitarianism,

00:00:18.760 --> 00:00:20.520
national socialism,

00:00:20.520 --> 00:00:21.720
Marxism,

00:00:21.720 --> 00:00:22.640
communism.

00:00:22.640 --> 00:00:24.960
All of these far right isms involve a lot

00:00:24.960 --> 00:00:27.800
of government control of the means of production.

00:00:27.800 --> 00:00:28.640
On the far left,

00:00:28.640 --> 00:00:29.920
you have Socialism,

00:00:29.920 --> 00:00:30.840
and Marxism,

00:00:30.840 --> 00:00:31.820
and Maoism.

00:00:31.820 --> 00:00:33.280
All of these isms, we're told,

00:00:33.280 --> 00:00:34.360
are fundamentally different

00:00:34.360 --> 00:00:35.840
than those on the right.

00:00:35.840 --> 00:00:37.640
But when you think about it,

00:00:37.640 --> 00:00:39.020
they sort of feel the same.

00:00:39.020 --> 00:00:40.560
You still have government control

00:00:40.560 --> 00:00:42.200
of businesses and factories,

00:00:42.200 --> 00:00:43.680
There's no freedom of speech,

00:00:43.680 --> 00:00:45.640
there's no freedom of association,

00:00:45.640 --> 00:00:47.080
there's hardly any freedom at all.

00:00:47.080 --> 00:00:48.680
Pundits talk about these things

00:00:48.680 --> 00:00:49.420
in terms of

00:00:49.420 --> 00:00:50.800
right vs left.

00:00:50.800 --> 00:00:53.480
This phony left right spectrum,

00:00:53.480 --> 00:00:55.080
it creates two problems.

00:00:55.080 --> 00:00:56.200
First of all,

00:00:56.200 --> 00:00:58.220
it keeps us fighting with each other,

00:00:58.240 --> 00:01:00.700
when we otherwise might find common values,

00:01:00.700 --> 00:01:02.760
we might find common ground,

00:01:02.760 --> 00:01:03.840
we might agree

00:01:03.840 --> 00:01:06.400
on the rules that hold civil society together.

00:01:06.400 --> 00:01:09.280
In truth, this whole left-right thing,

00:01:09.280 --> 00:01:10.440
it's the wrong way

00:01:10.460 --> 00:01:12.340
to think about political philosophy.

00:01:12.340 --> 00:01:14.020
Now many Americans say,

00:01:14.020 --> 00:01:15.380
I'm not left or right,

00:01:15.380 --> 00:01:16.620
I'm in the middle.

00:01:16.620 --> 00:01:17.345
I like

00:01:17.345 --> 00:01:19.280
bi-partisanship.

00:01:19.280 --> 00:01:20.080
Trouble is,

00:01:20.080 --> 00:01:22.980
when Republicans and Democrats agree,

00:01:22.980 --> 00:01:24.060
that usually means

00:01:24.060 --> 00:01:25.180
they've agreed to spend

00:01:25.200 --> 00:01:27.060
more of your money.

00:01:27.060 --> 00:01:29.340
That's what the politicians mean when they say,

00:01:29.340 --> 00:01:30.880
we're meeting in the middle.

00:01:30.880 --> 00:01:33.240
This celebrated middle of the road

00:01:33.280 --> 00:01:35.660
-- where Republicans collude with Democrats

00:01:35.660 --> 00:01:36.600
to say,

00:01:36.600 --> 00:01:37.900
bail out Wall Street,

00:01:37.900 --> 00:01:40.440
this can't be where the good stuff comes from,

00:01:40.440 --> 00:01:41.300
can it?

00:01:41.300 --> 00:01:42.060
No,

00:01:42.060 --> 00:01:43.300
most of the good stuff happens

00:01:43.300 --> 00:01:45.200
outside politics.

00:01:45.240 --> 00:01:47.240
It comes from millions of free people

00:01:47.240 --> 00:01:48.680
working together,

00:01:48.680 --> 00:01:50.320
voluntarily.

00:01:50.340 --> 00:01:53.480
America has been spared totalitarism and the

00:01:53.480 --> 00:01:56.260
other worst isms of the world.

00:01:56.260 --> 00:01:57.280
Capitalism

00:01:57.280 --> 00:02:00.040
is mostly good, because it's voluntary.

00:02:00.040 --> 00:02:00.680
But

00:02:00.680 --> 00:02:03.740
it's not if it's crony capitalism,

00:02:03.800 --> 00:02:05.000
crapitalism,

00:02:05.020 --> 00:02:06.280
corporatism.

00:02:06.280 --> 00:02:07.300
Corporatism.

00:02:07.300 --> 00:02:10.700
This is big business in cahoots with big government,

00:02:10.700 --> 00:02:11.880
fixing prices,

00:02:11.880 --> 00:02:12.860
raising costs,

00:02:12.860 --> 00:02:15.180
screwing the competition.

00:02:15.200 --> 00:02:16.280
This is pretty much where we

00:02:16.280 --> 00:02:17.360
are today.

00:02:17.360 --> 00:02:19.640
We got to big government corporatism

00:02:19.700 --> 00:02:21.500
with the help of experts,

00:02:21.500 --> 00:02:22.840
technocrats,

00:02:22.840 --> 00:02:23.780
people who say,

00:02:23.800 --> 00:02:25.360
we don't have any isms,

00:02:25.360 --> 00:02:25.891
we just

00:02:25.891 --> 00:02:27.560
want to do what works.

00:02:27.560 --> 00:02:31.840
I am not an ideologue.

00:02:31.840 --> 00:02:32.600
I'm not.

00:02:32.600 --> 00:02:34.640
Technocratic progressivism like espoused

00:02:34.640 --> 00:02:37.120
by Barack Obama and his cohorts

00:02:37.120 --> 00:02:38.980
is still an ism.

00:02:39.000 --> 00:02:41.500
We'll get to progressivism in this series.

00:02:41.500 --> 00:02:43.280
Yes, this is a series

00:02:43.280 --> 00:02:45.400
on different forms of government,

00:02:45.400 --> 00:02:47.900
the isms of the left and the right,

00:02:47.900 --> 00:02:50.060
but also the alternative.

00:02:50.060 --> 00:02:52.140
We're going to talk about liberty.

00:02:52.140 --> 00:02:54.640
We're going to talk about people cooperating.

00:02:54.640 --> 00:02:57.020
We're going to talk about entrepreneurship,

00:02:57.020 --> 00:02:59.760
and all of the really cool things that happen

00:02:59.760 --> 00:03:01.340
when people are left free.

00:03:01.340 --> 00:03:02.820
Kibbe's bottom line:

00:03:02.820 --> 00:03:04.180
I'll be on your side

00:03:04.180 --> 00:03:05.740
as long as you don't hurt people

00:03:05.740 --> 00:03:07.240
and you don't take their stuff.

00:03:07.240 --> 00:03:09.100
That's a political philosophy

00:03:09.100 --> 00:03:10.480
to get behind.

